
# Only produce additional .md file if asked or necessary, for documentary purpose .md, place them under docs folder, if no such folder exists in the working dirctory, create one, and keep the files in such folder ordered by having a number at the begining of all names.
# Avoid running training commands on your own, provide command and have me run it

# All project documentation files in the docs/ folder follow a chronological numbering system: ##_descriptive_topic_name.md. Files are numbered from 01 to 25 in the order they were created during the project's development, providing a historical timeline of implementation. Each filename uses lowercase with underscores (snake_case) and a descriptive name that clearly indicates the content (e.g., 15_llama3_gqa_scaling_law_implementation.md, 25_gpt2_llama3_scaling_law_analysis.md). The docs/README.md serves as a master index, grouping documents into phases (Phase 1: Setup & Foundation [01-04], Phase 2: Architecture Development [05-11], etc.) with quick navigation links and brief descriptions. When adding new documentation, assign the next sequential number (26, 27, etc.), use a clear descriptive name that captures the document's purpose, and update the docs/README.md to include the new file in the appropriate phase with a one-line description. This system maintains chronological traceability while making it easy to find specific topics.

# Prefer modular solutions over monolithic functions